#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM gratis tentang informasi dan komputasi kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bloch sphere"
msgstr "Bola Bloch"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There's a useful geometric way to represent qubit states known as the *Bloch sphere*.\n"
"It's very convenient, but unfortunately it only works for qubits — the analogous representation no longer corresponds to a spherical object once we have three or more classical states of our system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada cara geometris yang berguna untuk merepresentasikan keadaan qubit yang dikenal sebagai *bola Bloch*.\n"
"Ini sangat praktis, tetapi sayangnya hanya berfungsi untuk qubit — representasi analognya tidak lagi bersesuaian dengan objek berbentuk bola setelah kita memiliki tiga atau lebih keadaan klasik dari sistem kita.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qubit states as points on a sphere {#qubit-states-as-points-on-a-sphere}"
msgstr "Keadaan qubit sebagai titik pada bola {#qubit-states-as-points-on-a-sphere}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's start by thinking about a quantum state vector of a qubit: $\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
"We can restrict our attention to vectors for which $\\alpha$ is a nonnegative real number because every qubit state vector is equivalent up to a global phase to one for which $\\alpha \\geq 0$.\n"
"This allows us to write\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita mulai dengan memikirkan vektor keadaan kuantum dari qubit: $\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Kita bisa membatasi perhatian pada vektor di mana $\\alpha$ adalah bilangan real non-negatif karena setiap vektor keadaan qubit setara sampai fase global dengan satu di mana $\\alpha \\geq 0.$\n"
"Ini memungkinkan kita menulis\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\cos\\bigl(\\theta/2\\bigr) \\vert 0\\rangle + e^{i\\phi} \\sin\\bigl(\\theta/2\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\cos\\bigl(\\theta/2\\bigr) \\vert 0\\rangle + e^{i\\phi} \\sin\\bigl(\\theta/2\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for two real numbers $\\theta \\in [0,\\pi]$ and $\\phi\\in[0,2\\pi)$.\n"
"Here, we're allowing $\\theta$ to range from $0$ to $\\pi$ and dividing by $2$ in the argument of sine and cosine because this is a conventional way to parameterize vectors of this sort, and it will make things simpler a bit later on.\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk dua bilangan real $\\theta \\in [0,\\pi]$ dan $\\phi\\in[0,2\\pi)$.\n"
"Di sini, kita mengizinkan $\\theta$ berkisar dari $0$ ke $\\pi$ dan membaginya dengan $2$ dalam argumen sinus dan kosinus karena ini adalah cara konvensional untuk memarameterisasi vektor-vektor seperti ini, dan ini akan menyederhanakan segalanya sedikit kemudian.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, it isn't quite the case that the numbers $\\theta$ and $\\phi$ are uniquely determined by a given quantum state vector $\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle$, but it is nearly so.\n"
"In particular, if $\\beta = 0$, then $\\theta = 0$ and it doesn't make any difference what value $\\phi$ takes, so it can be chosen arbitrarily.\n"
"Similarly, if $\\alpha = 0$, then $\\theta = \\pi$, and once again $\\phi$ is irrelevant (as our state is equivalent to $e^{i\\phi}\\vert 1\\rangle$ for any $\\phi$ up to a global phase).\n"
"If, however, neither $\\alpha$ nor $\\beta$ is zero, then there's a unique choice for the pair $(\\theta,\\phi)$ for which $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is equivalent to $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle$ up to a global phase.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, tidak sepenuhnya benar bahwa bilangan $\\theta$ dan $\\phi$ ditentukan secara unik oleh vektor keadaan kuantum $\\alpha \\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta \\vert 1\\rangle$, tetapi hampir demikian.\n"
"Khususnya, jika $\\beta = 0$, maka $\\theta = 0$ dan tidak ada bedanya nilai $\\phi$ yang diambil, sehingga bisa dipilih secara arbitrer.\n"
"Demikian pula, jika $\\alpha = 0$, maka $\\theta = \\pi$, dan sekali lagi $\\phi$ tidak relevan (karena keadaan kita setara dengan $e^{i\\phi}\\vert 1\\rangle$ untuk $\\phi$ manapun sampai fase global).\n"
"Namun, jika $\\alpha$ maupun $\\beta$ tidak nol, maka ada pilihan unik untuk pasangan $(\\theta,\\phi)$ di mana $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ setara dengan $\\alpha\\vert 0\\rangle + \\beta\\vert 1\\rangle$ sampai fase global.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, let's consider the density matrix representation of this state.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, mari kita pertimbangkan representasi matriks densitas dari keadaan ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos^2(\\theta/2) & e^{-i\\phi}\\cos(\\theta/2)\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"e^{i\\phi}\\cos(\\theta/2)\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\sin^2(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos^2(\\theta/2) & e^{-i\\phi}\\cos(\\theta/2)\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"e^{i\\phi}\\cos(\\theta/2)\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\sin^2(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can use some trigonometric identities,\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa menggunakan beberapa identitas trigonometri,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\cos^2(\\theta/2) = \\frac{1 + \\cos(\\theta)}{2},\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\sin^2(\\theta/2) = \\frac{1 - \\cos(\\theta)}{2},\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) \\sin(\\theta/2) = \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2},\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\cos^2(\\theta/2) = \\frac{1 + \\cos(\\theta)}{2},\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\sin^2(\\theta/2) = \\frac{1 - \\cos(\\theta)}{2},\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) \\sin(\\theta/2) = \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2},\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "as well as the formula $e^{i\\phi} = \\cos(\\phi) + i\\sin(\\phi)$, to simplify the density matrix as follows.\n"
msgstr "serta rumus $e^{i\\phi} = \\cos(\\phi) + i\\sin(\\phi)$, untuk menyederhanakan matriks densitas sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 + \\cos(\\theta) & (\\cos(\\phi) - i \\sin(\\phi)) \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"(\\cos(\\phi) + i \\sin(\\phi)) \\sin(\\theta) & 1 - \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 + \\cos(\\theta) & (\\cos(\\phi) - i \\sin(\\phi)) \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"(\\cos(\\phi) + i \\sin(\\phi)) \\sin(\\theta) & 1 - \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This makes it easy to express this density matrix as a linear combination of the Pauli matrices:\n"
msgstr "Ini memudahkan untuk mengekspresikan matriks densitas ini sebagai kombinasi linear dari matriks Pauli:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    0 & 1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"  \\quad\n"
"  \\sigma_x =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    0 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    1 & 0\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"  \\quad\n"
"  \\sigma_y =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    0 & -i\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    i & 0\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"  \\quad\n"
"  \\sigma_z =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    0 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    0 & 1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"  \\quad\n"
"  \\sigma_x =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    0 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    1 & 0\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"  \\quad\n"
"  \\sigma_y =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    0 & -i\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    i & 0\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"  \\quad\n"
"  \\sigma_z =\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"    1 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"    0 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specifically, we conclude that\n"
msgstr "Secara khusus, kita menyimpulkan bahwa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sin(\\theta) \\cos(\\phi)\\sigma_x + \\sin(\\theta)\\sin(\\phi) \\sigma_y + \\cos(\\theta) \\sigma_z}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sin(\\theta) \\cos(\\phi)\\sigma_x + \\sin(\\theta)\\sin(\\phi) \\sigma_y + \\cos(\\theta) \\sigma_z}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The coefficients of $\\sigma_x$, $\\sigma_y$, and $\\sigma_z$ in the numerator of this expression are all real numbers, so we can collect them together to form a vector in an ordinary, three-dimensional Euclidean space.\n"
msgstr "Koefisien dari $\\sigma_x,$ $\\sigma_y,$ dan $\\sigma_z$ dalam pembilang ekspresi ini semuanya adalah bilangan real, sehingga kita bisa mengumpulkan mereka untuk membentuk vektor dalam ruang Euclidean tiga-dimensi biasa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl(\\sin(\\theta) \\cos(\\phi), \\sin(\\theta)\\sin(\\phi), \\cos(\\theta)\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl(\\sin(\\theta) \\cos(\\phi), \\sin(\\theta)\\sin(\\phi), \\cos(\\theta)\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In fact, this is a unit vector.\n"
"Using *spherical coordinates* it can be written as $(1,\\theta,\\phi)$.\n"
"The first coordinate, $1$, represents the *radius* or *radial distance* (which is always $1$ in this case), $\\theta$ represents the *polar angle*, and $\\phi$ represents the *azimuthal angle*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Faktanya, ini adalah vektor satuan.\n"
"Menggunakan *koordinat bola* bisa ditulis sebagai $(1,\\theta,\\phi).$\n"
"Koordinat pertama, $1,$ mewakili *radius* atau *jarak radial* (yang selalu $1$ dalam kasus ini), $\\theta$ mewakili *sudut polar*, dan $\\phi$ mewakili *sudut azimut*.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In words, thinking about a sphere as the planet Earth, the polar angle $\\theta$ is how far we rotate south from the north pole to reach the point being described, from $0$ to $\\pi = 180^{\\circ}$, while the azimuthal angle $\\phi$ is how far we rotate east from the prime meridian, from $0$ to $2\\pi = 360^{\\circ}$.\n"
"This assumes that we define the prime meridian to be the curve on the surface of the sphere from one pole to the other that passes through the positive $x$-axis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan kata lain, memikirkan sebuah bola sebagai planet Bumi, sudut polar $\\theta$ adalah seberapa jauh kita berputar ke selatan dari kutub utara untuk mencapai titik yang dijelaskan, dari $0$ hingga $\\pi = 180^{\\circ}$, sementara sudut azimut $\\phi$ adalah seberapa jauh kita berputar ke timur dari meridian utama, dari $0$ hingga $2\\pi = 360^{\\circ}$.\n"
"Ini mengasumsikan bahwa kita mendefinisikan meridian utama sebagai kurva pada permukaan bola dari satu kutub ke kutub lain yang melewati sumbu $x$ positif.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Illustration of a point on the unit 2-sphere in terms of its spherical coordinates.](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/spherical-coordinates.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Ilustrasi titik pada bola satuan 2 dalam hal koordinat bolanya.](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/spherical-coordinates.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every point on the sphere can be described in this way — which is to say that the points we obtain when we range over all possible pure states of a qubit correspond precisely to a sphere in $3$ real dimensions.\n"
"(This sphere is typically called the *unit $2$-sphere* because the surface of this sphere is two-dimensional.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap titik pada bola bisa dideskripsikan dengan cara ini — yang berarti bahwa titik-titik yang kita peroleh saat kita merentang semua keadaan murni yang mungkin dari sebuah qubit bersesuaian tepat dengan bola dalam $3$ dimensi real.\n"
"(Bola ini biasanya disebut *bola satuan $2$* karena permukaan bola ini berdimensi dua.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When we associate points on the unit $2$-sphere with pure states of qubits, we obtain the *Bloch sphere* representation these states.\n"
msgstr "Ketika kita mengasosiasikan titik-titik pada bola satuan $2$ dengan keadaan murni qubit, kita mendapatkan representasi *bola Bloch* dari keadaan-keadaan ini.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Six important examples {#six-important-examples}"
msgstr "Enam contoh penting {#six-important-examples}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*The standard basis* $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\vert 1\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"Let's start with the state $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"As a density matrix it can be written like this.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Basis standar* $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\vert 1\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"Mari kita mulai dengan keadaan $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"Sebagai matriks densitas bisa ditulis seperti ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   By collecting the coefficients of the Pauli matrices in the numerator, we see that the corresponding point on the unit $2$-sphere using Cartesian coordinates is $(0,0,1)$.\n"
"   In spherical coordinates this point is $(1,0,\\phi)$, where $\\phi$ can be any angle.\n"
"   This is consistent with the expression\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dengan mengumpulkan koefisien dari matriks Pauli dalam pembilang, kita melihat bahwa titik yang bersesuaian pada bola satuan $2$ menggunakan koordinat Cartesian adalah $(0,0,1)$.\n"
"   Dalam koordinat bola titik ini adalah $(1,0,\\phi)$, di mana $\\phi$ bisa berupa sudut manapun.\n"
"   Ini konsisten dengan ekspresi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert 0\\rangle = \\cos(0) \\vert 0\\rangle + e^{i \\phi} \\sin(0) \\vert 1\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert 0\\rangle = \\cos(0) \\vert 0\\rangle + e^{i \\phi} \\sin(0) \\vert 1\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   which also works for any $\\phi$.\n"
"   Intuitively speaking, the polar angle $\\theta$ is zero, so we're at the north pole of the Bloch sphere, where the azimuthal angle is irrelevant.\n"
msgstr ""
"   yang juga berlaku untuk $\\phi$ manapun.\n"
"   Secara intuitif, sudut polar $\\theta$ adalah nol, sehingga kita berada di kutub utara bola Bloch, di mana sudut azimut tidak relevan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Along similar lines, the density matrix for the state $\\vert 1\\rangle$ can be written like so.\n"
msgstr "   Dengan cara yang sama, matriks densitas untuk keadaan $\\vert 1\\rangle$ dapat ditulis seperti ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   This time the Cartesian coordinates are $(0,0,-1)$. In spherical coordinates this point is $(1,\\pi,\\phi)$ where $\\phi$ can be any angle. In this case the polar angle is all the way to $\\pi$, so we're at the south pole where the azimuthal angle is again irrelevant.\n"
msgstr "   Kali ini koordinat Cartesian adalah $(0,0,-1)$. Dalam koordinat bola titik ini adalah $(1,\\pi,\\phi)$ di mana $\\phi$ bisa berupa sudut manapun. Dalam kasus ini sudut polar berada di $\\pi$, sehingga kita berada di kutub selatan di mana sudut azimut kembali tidak relevan.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*The basis $\\{\\vert + \\rangle, \\vert - \\rangle\\}$.*\n"
"We have these expressions for the density matrices corresponding to these states.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Basis $\\{\\vert + \\rangle, \\vert - \\rangle\\}$.*\n"
"Kita memiliki ekspresi-ekspresi ini untuk matriks densitas yang bersesuaian dengan keadaan-keadaan ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\vert {+} \\rangle\\langle {+} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_x}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\vert {-} \\rangle\\langle {-} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\sigma_x}{2}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\vert {+} \\rangle\\langle {+} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_x}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\vert {-} \\rangle\\langle {-} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\sigma_x}{2}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The corresponding points on the unit $2$-sphere have Cartesian coordinates $(1,0,0)$ and $(-1,0,0)$,\n"
"   and spherical coordinates $(1,\\pi/2,0)$ and $(1,\\pi/2,\\pi)$, respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Titik-titik yang bersesuaian pada bola satuan $2$ memiliki koordinat Cartesian $(1,0,0)$ dan $(-1,0,0)$,\n"
"   dan koordinat bola $(1,\\pi/2,0)$ dan $(1,\\pi/2,\\pi)$, masing-masing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   In words, $\\vert +\\rangle$ corresponds to the point where the positive $x$-axis intersects the unit $2$-sphere and $\\vert -\\rangle$ corresponds to the point where the negative $x$-axis intersects it. More intuitively, $\\vert +\\rangle$ is on the equator of the Bloch sphere where it meets the prime meridian, and $\\vert - \\rangle$ is on the equator on the opposite side of the sphere.\n"
msgstr "   Dengan kata lain, $\\vert +\\rangle$ bersesuaian dengan titik di mana sumbu $x$ positif berpotongan dengan bola satuan $2$ dan $\\vert -\\rangle$ bersesuaian dengan titik di mana sumbu $x$ negatif berpotongan dengannya. Lebih intuitif, $\\vert +\\rangle$ berada di khatulistiwa bola Bloch tempat ia bertemu dengan meridian utama, dan $\\vert - \\rangle$ berada di khatulistiwa di sisi bola yang berlawanan.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*The basis* $\\{\\vert {+i} \\rangle, \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\}$.\n"
"As we saw earlier in the lesson, these two states are defined like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Basis* $\\{\\vert {+i} \\rangle, \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\}$.\n"
"Seperti yang kita lihat sebelumnya dalam pelajaran, dua keadaan ini didefinisikan seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\vert {+i} \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\vert {-i} \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\vert {+i} \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\vert {-i} \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   This time we have these expressions.\n"
msgstr "   Kali ini kita memiliki ekspresi-ekspresi ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_y}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\sigma_y}{2}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\vert {+i} \\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_y}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i} \\vert & = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\sigma_y}{2}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The corresponding points on the unit $2$-sphere have Cartesian coordinates $(0,1,0)$ and $(0,-1,0)$,\n"
"   and spherical coordinates $(1,\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$ and $(1,\\pi/2,3\\pi/2)$, respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Titik-titik yang bersesuaian pada bola satuan $2$ memiliki koordinat Cartesian $(0,1,0)$ dan $(0,-1,0)$,\n"
"   dan koordinat bola $(1,\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$ dan $(1,\\pi/2,3\\pi/2)$, masing-masing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   In words, $\\vert {+i} \\rangle$ corresponds to the point where the positive $y$-axis intersects the unit $2$-sphere and $\\vert {-i} \\rangle$ to the point where the negative $y$-axis intersects it.\n"
msgstr "   Dengan kata lain, $\\vert {+i} \\rangle$ bersesuaian dengan titik di mana sumbu $y$ positif berpotongan dengan bola satuan $2$ dan $\\vert {-i} \\rangle$ bersesuaian dengan titik di mana sumbu $y$ negatif berpotongan dengannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Illustration of six examples of pure states on the Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/six-Bloch-sphere-points.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Ilustrasi enam contoh keadaan murni pada bola Bloch](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/six-Bloch-sphere-points.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here's another class of quantum state vectors that has appeared from time to time throughout this series, including previously in this lesson.\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah kelas lain dari vektor keadaan kuantum yang telah muncul dari waktu ke waktu sepanjang seri ini, termasuk sebelumnya dalam pelajaran ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_{\\alpha} \\rangle = \\cos(\\alpha) \\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\alpha) \\vert 1\\rangle \\qquad \\text{(for $\\alpha \\in [0,\\pi)$)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_{\\alpha} \\rangle = \\cos(\\alpha) \\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\alpha) \\vert 1\\rangle \\qquad \\text{(for $\\alpha \\in [0,\\pi)$)}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The density matrix representation of each of these states is as follows.\n"
msgstr "Representasi matriks densitas dari masing-masing keadaan ini adalah sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_{\\alpha} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos^2(\\alpha) & \\cos(\\alpha)\\sin(\\alpha)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\alpha)\\sin(\\alpha) & \\sin^2(\\alpha)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sin(2\\alpha) \\sigma_x + \\cos(2\\alpha) \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_{\\alpha} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos^2(\\alpha) & \\cos(\\alpha)\\sin(\\alpha)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\alpha)\\sin(\\alpha) & \\sin^2(\\alpha)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sin(2\\alpha) \\sigma_x + \\cos(2\\alpha) \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following figure illustrates the corresponding points on the Bloch sphere for a few choices for $\\alpha$.\n"
msgstr "Gambar berikut mengilustrasikan titik-titik yang bersesuaian pada bola Bloch untuk beberapa pilihan $\\alpha$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Illustration of real-valued qubit state vectors on the Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/real-Bloch-sphere-points.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Ilustrasi vektor keadaan qubit bernilai real pada bola Bloch](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/real-Bloch-sphere-points.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convex combinations of points {#convex-combinations-of-points}"
msgstr "Kombinasi konveks dari titik-titik {#convex-combinations-of-points}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similar to what we have already discussed for density matrices, we can take convex combinations of points on the Bloch sphere to obtain representations of qubit density matrices.\n"
"In general, this results in points *inside* of the Bloch sphere, which represent density matrices of states that are not pure.\n"
"Sometimes we refer to the *Bloch ball* when we wish to be explicit about the inclusion of points inside of the Bloch sphere as representations of qubit density matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mirip dengan apa yang sudah kita bahas untuk matriks densitas, kita bisa mengambil kombinasi konveks dari titik-titik pada bola Bloch untuk mendapatkan representasi dari matriks densitas qubit.\n"
"Secara umum, ini menghasilkan titik-titik *di dalam* bola Bloch, yang mewakili matriks densitas dari keadaan yang tidak murni.\n"
"Kadang-kadang kita menyebut *bola padat Bloch* (Bloch ball) ketika kita ingin eksplisit tentang penyertaan titik-titik di dalam bola Bloch sebagai representasi dari matriks densitas qubit.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, we've seen that the density matrix $\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbb{I}$, which represents the completely mixed state of a qubit, can be written in these two alternative ways:\n"
msgstr "Misalnya, kita sudah melihat bahwa matriks densitas $\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbb{I}$, yang mewakili keadaan campuran sempurna dari sebuah qubit, bisa ditulis dalam dua cara alternatif ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We also have\n"
msgstr "Kita juga memiliki\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert {+i}\\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i}\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert {+i}\\rangle\\langle {+i} \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert {-i} \\rangle\\langle {-i}\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and more generally we can use any two orthogonal qubit state vectors (which will always correspond to two antipodal points on the Bloch sphere).\n"
"If we average the corresponding points on the Bloch sphere in a similar way, we obtain the same point, which in this case is at the center of the sphere.\n"
"This is consistent with the observation that\n"
msgstr ""
"dan lebih umumnya kita bisa menggunakan dua vektor keadaan qubit ortogonal manapun (yang akan selalu bersesuaian dengan dua titik antipodal pada bola Bloch).\n"
"Jika kita merata-rata titik-titik yang bersesuaian pada bola Bloch dengan cara yang sama, kita mendapatkan titik yang sama, yang dalam kasus ini berada di pusat bola.\n"
"Ini konsisten dengan observasi bahwa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + 0 \\cdot \\sigma_x + 0 \\cdot \\sigma_y + 0 \\cdot \\sigma_z}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I} = \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + 0 \\cdot \\sigma_x + 0 \\cdot \\sigma_y + 0 \\cdot \\sigma_z}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "giving us the Cartesian coordinates $(0,0,0)$.\n"
msgstr "memberi kita koordinat Cartesian $(0,0,0)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A different example concerning convex combinations of Bloch sphere points is the one discussed in the previous subsection.\n"
msgstr "Contoh berbeda tentang kombinasi konveks dari titik-titik bola Bloch adalah yang dibahas dalam subbagian sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle + \\vert\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert +\n"
"\\sin^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle + \\vert\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert +\n"
"\\sin^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8} \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following figure illustrates these two different ways of obtaining this density matrix as a convex combination of pure states.\n"
msgstr "Gambar berikut mengilustrasikan dua cara berbeda untuk mendapatkan matriks densitas ini sebagai kombinasi konveks dari keadaan murni.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Illustration of the average of the zero state and the plus state on the Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/Bloch-sphere-zero-plus-average.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Ilustrasi rata-rata keadaan nol dan keadaan plus pada bola Bloch](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/density-matrices/Bloch-sphere-zero-plus-average.avif)\n"
